{"id":"7da7ff11e397ca55","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-singular-value.md","title":"Singular Value","display":"df-singular-value — Singular Value","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-singular-value","aliases":["58-df-singular-value"],"display":"df-singular-value — Singular Value","depends_on":["[[58-df-compact-operator]]","[[58-df-bounded-operator]]","[[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-dimension.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-field.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-singular-value"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-singular-value</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-singular-value — Singular Value"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"28999e0c83253377\" href=\"?note=28999e0c83253377\" title=\"58-df-compact-operator\">58-df-compact-operator</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2ad9c248fe18df37\" href=\"?note=2ad9c248fe18df37\" title=\"58-df-bounded-operator\">58-df-bounded-operator</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md\">../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"522587a7fec6816a\" href=\"?note=522587a7fec6816a\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-dimension.md\">../batch09/58-df-dimension.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"1eb4a89b005d9cda\" href=\"?note=1eb4a89b005d9cda\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-field.md\">../batch13/58-df-field.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,K,T,s,n\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(H,K,T,s,n\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5\\cup V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5\\cup V^2\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CompactOperatorStructure}_S:V^{11}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{CompactOperatorStructure}_S:V^{11}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"28999e0c83253377\" href=\"?note=28999e0c83253377\" title=\"58-df-compact-operator\">58-df-compact-operator</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S:V^{10}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S:V^{10}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{OpNorm}:V^5\\to[0,\\infty]\">\\(\\operatorname{OpNorm}:V^5\\to[0,\\infty]\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"2ad9c248fe18df37\" href=\"?note=2ad9c248fe18df37\" title=\"58-df-bounded-operator\">58-df-bounded-operator</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Dimension}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Dimension}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"522587a7fec6816a\" href=\"?note=522587a7fec6816a\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-dimension.md\">../batch09/58-df-dimension.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Field}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Field}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"1eb4a89b005d9cda\" href=\"?note=1eb4a89b005d9cda\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-field.md\">../batch13/58-df-field.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Span}_{\\mathbb C}:V^5\\to V\">\\(\\operatorname{Span}_{\\mathbb C}:V^5\\to V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{OperatorDifference}:V^5\\to V\">\\(\\operatorname{OperatorDifference}:V^5\\to V\\)</span> (local set-coded operators defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SingularValue}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\operatorname{SingularValue}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> (defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}value\\text{-}span} \\vdash \\operatorname{Span}_{\\mathbb C}(E;K,+_K,\\odot_K,0_K)\\coloneqq\\bigcap\\{W\\subseteq K:E\\subseteq W\\land0_K\\in W\\land\\forall x,y\\in W\\;(+_K(\\langle x,y\\rangle)\\in W)\\land\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x\\in W\\;(\\odot_K(\\langle\\lambda,x\\rangle)\\in W)\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}value\\text{-}span} \\vdash \\operatorname{Span}_{\\mathbb C}(E;K,+_K,\\odot_K,0_K)\\coloneqq\\bigcap\\{W\\subseteq K:E\\subseteq W\\land0_K\\in W\\land\\forall x,y\\in W\\;(+_K(\\langle x,y\\rangle)\\in W)\\land\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathbb C\\;\\forall x\\in W\\;(\\odot_K(\\langle\\lambda,x\\rangle)\\in W)\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}value\\text{-}difference} \\vdash \\operatorname{OperatorDifference}(T,F;H,+_K,\\odot_K)\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,+_K(\\langle T(x),\\odot_K(\\langle-1,F(x)\\rangle)\\rangle)\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}value\\text{-}difference} \\vdash \\operatorname{OperatorDifference}(T,F;H,+_K,\\odot_K)\\coloneqq\\{\\langle x,+_K(\\langle T(x),\\odot_K(\\langle-1,F(x)\\rangle)\\rangle)\\rangle:x\\in H\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}value\\text{-}predicate}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SingularValue}_S(s,n,T,H,K)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\exists B_H,B_K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0_{\\mathbb C},1_{\\mathbb C},0_K,d_K\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\\\\n&amp;\\mathrm{Field}_S(\\mathbb C,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0_{\\mathbb C},1_{\\mathbb C})\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,\\mathbb C,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(K,B_K,\\mathbb C,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\land0_K\\in K\\land\\forall y\\in K\\;(+_K(\\langle0_K,y\\rangle)=y)\\land\\forall y,z\\in K\\;(d_K(y,z)=\\nu_{B_K}(+_K(\\langle y,\\odot_K(\\langle-1,z\\rangle)\\rangle)))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{CompactOperatorStructure}_S(T;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K,d_K;\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&amp;\\land s=\\inf\\Bigl\\{\\operatorname{OpNorm}(\\operatorname{OperatorDifference}(T,F;H,+_K,\\odot_K);H,\\nu_{B_H},K,\\nu_{B_K}):F\\in V\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S(F;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\exists m\\in n\\;\\exists W\\in V\\;\\Bigl(W=\\operatorname{Span}_{\\mathbb C}(F[H];K,+_K,\\odot_K,0_K)\\land\\mathrm{Dimension}_S\\!\\left(m,\\left\\langle W,\\mathbb C,+_K\\!\\upharpoonright W^2,\\odot_K\\!\\upharpoonright(\\mathbb C\\times W),+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0_{\\mathbb C},1_{\\mathbb C},0_K\\right\\rangle\\right)\\Bigr)\\Bigr\\}\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}singular\\text{-}value\\text{-}predicate}\\vdash\n\\operatorname{SingularValue}_S(s,n,T,H,K)\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\nn\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\exists B_H,B_K,+_H,\\odot_H,+_K,\\odot_K,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0_{\\mathbb C},1_{\\mathbb C},0_K,d_K\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\\\\\n&amp;\\mathrm{Field}_S(\\mathbb C,+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0_{\\mathbb C},1_{\\mathbb C})\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_H,\\mathbb C,+_H,\\odot_H)\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(K,B_K,\\mathbb C,+_K,\\odot_K)\\\\\n&amp;\\land0_K\\in K\\land\\forall y\\in K\\;(+_K(\\langle0_K,y\\rangle)=y)\\land\\forall y,z\\in K\\;(d_K(y,z)=\\nu_{B_K}(+_K(\\langle y,\\odot_K(\\langle-1,z\\rangle)\\rangle)))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{CompactOperatorStructure}_S(T;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K,d_K;\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&amp;\\land s=\\inf\\Bigl\\{\\operatorname{OpNorm}(\\operatorname{OperatorDifference}(T,F;H,+_K,\\odot_K);H,\\nu_{B_H},K,\\nu_{B_K}):F\\in V\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\mathrm{BoundedOperatorStructure}_S(F;H,\\nu_{B_H},+_H,\\odot_H;K,\\nu_{B_K},+_K,\\odot_K;\\mathbb C)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\exists m\\in n\\;\\exists W\\in V\\;\\Bigl(W=\\operatorname{Span}_{\\mathbb C}(F[H];K,+_K,\\odot_K,0_K)\\land\\mathrm{Dimension}_S\\!\\left(m,\\left\\langle W,\\mathbb C,+_K\\!\\upharpoonright W^2,\\odot_K\\!\\upharpoonright(\\mathbb C\\times W),+_{\\mathbb C},\\cdot_{\\mathbb C},0_{\\mathbb C},1_{\\mathbb C},0_K\\right\\rangle\\right)\\Bigr)\\Bigr\\}\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The predicate directly graphs the <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>th approximation number; it no longer depends on an unregistered partial operator <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s_n(T)\">\\(s_n(T)\\)</span>.  For compact <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span>, these numbers agree with the eigenvalues of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|T|=(T^*T)^{1/2}\">\\(|T|=(T^*T)^{1/2}\\)</span>, with multiplicity and trailing zeros.</li>\n<li>For a general bounded operator, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|T|\">\\(|T|\\)</span> may have continuous spectrum, so an eigenvalue enumeration need not exist.</li>\n<li>The dimension source is two-place and consumes a complete vector-space code. The corrected formula builds that code for the range span and measures <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T-F\">\\(T-F\\)</span> using the same Hilbert norms as compactness, eliminating both the former three-place call and incompatible existential witnesses.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-compact-operator","status":"resolved","id":"28999e0c83253377","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-compact-operator]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bounded-operator","status":"resolved","id":"2ad9c248fe18df37","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bounded-operator]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-dimension.md","status":"resolved","id":"522587a7fec6816a","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-dimension.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../bat